    [BugFix][CI] Restore GLM5_1_W4A4_A5 to the V1 server config (#19055)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    #17681 moved GLM5_1_W4A4_A5 onto a Model Runner V2 server shape (TP=2,
    prefill-context-parallel-size=4, HCCL_BUFFSIZE=1024,
    gpu-memory-utilization=0.90, CLI EPLB). A follow-up only pinned
    VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0. V1 rejects prefill context parallel greater
    than 1, so the A5 nightly fails before the server starts.
    
    This puts the server config back to the last green V1 shape (b600661)
    and keeps the V1 pin, because main now defaults to Model Runner V2:
    
    - tensor-parallel-size 2 + PCP 4 → 8, PCP removed
    - HCCL_BUFFSIZE 1024 → 400
    - DYNAMIC_EPLB=true restored
    - gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 → 0.95
    - --enable-eplb / --eplb-config removed
    - additional-config restored to enable_dsa_cp plus the dynamic EPLB
    block
    
    GLM5_1_W4A4_A5_weekly.yaml was not changed by #17681.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Nightly server arguments for GLM5_1_W4A4_A5 only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Diff against b600661 is only VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER: "0".
    - Parsed the yaml: runner pin 0, HCCL_BUFFSIZE=400, DYNAMIC_EPLB=true,
    TP=8, no PCP, no --enable-eplb, gpu-memory-utilization=0.95.
    - NPU coverage is /nightly GLM5_1_W4A4_A5 on this PR.
    
    - vLLM
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: yjyang62 <yangjinyang5@huawei.com>

